Title: SCSS Layout Ontology

Purpose: document how the layout partials map to our SCSS modules so the “purpose + empirical cards + CTA + any other layout” pattern stays consistent and responsive.

Sections:

1. Structure
   - Each major page segment (`intro`, `purpose`, `empiricals`, `memories`, `footer`) gets a `views/partials/` template plus a layout SCSS file under `src/scss/layout/`.
   - Layout SCSS files import `@use '../utils/mixins' as *` and `@use '../base/variables' as *` so they rely on the shared mixins/variables rather than duplicating color logic.
   - The entry point (`views/index.ejs`) includes the partials in source order but the purpose section may include the cards partial (the “empirical learnings” strip) if the content feels tightly coupled to that narrative.

2. Empirical layout
   - `views/partials/cards.ejs` renders the “Pull look : empirical learnings” carousel. Its SCSS lives in `src/scss/layout/_empirical.scss`, which defines `#cards`, `featured-card`, and `smaller-cards`.
   - All card panels use the `@include mist-panel()` mixin and `@include motion-link()` for links/headings so the “gray mist” depth effect stays uniform.
   - Cards are responsive: the grid uses `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px,1fr))`, and the featured card spans two columns only above the tablet breakpoint (`@include tablet-horizontal-large`).

3. Purpose section
   - `#purpose` extends `%section`, keeps a `min-height` tied to the viewport minus `--footer-height`, and hosts the animated `.phrase` loop plus `.button-group`.
   - The `.button-group` stays flexible/wrapped but both buttons extend `%button-base`, so their width/height remains identical across breakpoints.
   - Animate only the `color`/`text-shadow` of the phrases so none of the text fades out and the “hero idea” stays prominent.

4. Footer + cards relationship
   - The footer uses `@include brand-gradient()` for the background overlay and holds `#socials`; it must stay visually separate from the above cards block, so the cards partial includes its own spacing.
   - Layout rules require the cards section to live between `#purpose` and the footer (either via the purpose partial include or via `index.ejs`), ensuring the “empirical learnings” cards sit right below the CTA.

5. Utility reminder
   - When new layout utility classes (grid, card, responsive panel) are added, document them here and ensure their selectors appear in the matching layout SCSS file, not inside `_mixins.scss`. The mixins remain helpers; the layout files hold the semantic structure.

Use this file plus `scss-patterns.mdc` as the source of truth for future layout additions.
